      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_44878066",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image displays crumpled pieces of paper on a plain background, with overlaid text reading 'farmersonly.com... where white trash meet other white trash.' The visual metaphor of crumpled paper suggests discarded or worthless items, which is juxtaposed with the derogatory term 'white trash' to imply that the website is a space for people who are considered socially or morally inferior. This is a hateful meme as it uses a racialized slur ('white trash') to demean a specific group of people, promoting negative stereotypes and reinforcing harmful social divisions. The term 'white trash' is a derogatory label historically used to demean people of lower socioeconomic status, often targeting white individuals, and is rooted in racial and class-based prejudice. The meme's intent is to dehumanize and insult a group by associating them with trash, thereby fostering contempt and division.",
